You may wonder:

"Okay, I created a Servlet. Who runs it?"

Tomcat.

Tomcat is a Servlet container / web server that manages Servlets.

Think of Tomcat as a manager.

                 TOMCAT
                    |
        -------------------------
        |           |           |
   StudentServlet LoginServlet OrderServlet

Tomcat:

starts your web application
receives HTTP requests
finds the correct Servlet
creates/manages Servlet objects
calls doGet() / doPost()
sends the response back
Very simple analogy

Imagine:

Customer → Restaurant → Waiter → Kitchen

In web applications:

Browser → Tomcat → Servlet → Java logic

Tomcat is basically the environment that runs your Servlet.
